{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TwFyXuQkiYrE1qSnARPGcu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\texperiments:\n2\t  # === P0: Must-run for paper submission ===\n3\t\n4\t  - id: plan_001\n5\t    claim: [2]\n6\t    description: >\n7\t      Remove L0 exclusion constraint from solver, keep only max_2bit=8.\n8\t      Verify solver still assigns 8-bit to Layer 0 heads purely from profiling data.\n9\t      Strengthens narrative: \"solver automatically discovers sensitivity structure.\"\n10\t    priority: P0\n11\t    gpu_budget_hours: 1\n12\t    deps: []\n13\t    registry_id: exp_d_no_l0_exclusion\n14\t    model: Qwen2.5-7B\n15\t    eval: WikiText-2\n16\t\n17\t  - id: plan_002\n18\t    claim: [1, 2]\n19\t    description: >\n20\t      Replicate full pipeline on Llama-3.1-8B (GQA ratio 4:1 vs Qwen 7:1).\n21\t      Profile all KV heads, run constrained MCKP, evaluate PPL.\n22\t      Tests generalizability across different GQA ratios and architectures.\n23\t      Fallback if HF token unavailable: Yi-1.5-9B (non-gated, similar scale).\n24\t    priority: P0\n25\t    gpu_budget_hours: 4\n26\t    deps: []\n27\t    registry_id: null\n28\t    model: Llama-3.1-8B\n29\t    fallback_model: Yi-1.5-9B\n30\t    eval: WikiText-2\n31\t\n32\t  - id: plan_003\n33\t    claim: [1, 2]\n34\t    description: >\n35\t      Replicate full pipeline on Mistral-7B-v0.3.\n36\t      Different architecture family to establish cross-architecture validity.\n37\t    priority: P0\n38\t    gpu_budget_hours: 4\n39\t    deps: []\n40\t    registry_id: null\n41\t    model: Mistral-7B-v0.3\n42\t    eval: WikiText-2\n43\t\n44\t  - id: plan_004\n45\t    claim: [3]\n46\t    description: >\n47\t      Compounding effect characterization: sweep max_2bit from 0 to 112\n48\t      (steps: 0, 4, 8, 16, 24, 48, 75, 112) on Qwen2.5-7B.\n49\t      Plot PPL vs max_2bit to map the compounding threshold.\n50\t      Establishes the principled basis for cardinality constraint selection.\n51\t    priority: P0\n52\t    gpu_budget_hours: 3\n53\t    deps: []\n54\t    registry_id: null\n55\t    model: Qwen2.5-7B\n56\t    eval: WikiText-2\n57\t\n58\t  - id: plan_005\n59\t    claim: [2]\n60\t    description: >\n61\t      Budget sweep: test constrained MCKP at compression ratios 2×, 4×, 8×\n62\t      (budget = 0.5, 0.25, 0.125) on Qwen2.5-7B.\n63\t      Compare each against uniform baseline at same budget.\n64\t    priority: P0\n65\t    gpu_budget_hours: 3\n66\t    deps: []\n67\t    registry_id: null\n68\t    model: Qwen2.5-7B\n69\t    eval: WikiText-2\n70\t\n71\t  - id: plan_006\n72\t    claim: [1, 2]\n73\t    description: >\n74\t      High-resolution profiling: 64 seq × 2048 tokens (vs current 16×512).\n75\t      Rerun MCKP with hires profiles on Qwen2.5-7B.\n76\t      Tests whether better profiling discovers mid-layer heterogeneity\n77\t      and improves solver allocation beyond current results.\n78\t    priority: P0\n79\t    gpu_budget_hours: 3\n80\t    deps: []\n81\t    registry_id: null\n82\t    model: Qwen2.5-7B\n83\t    eval: WikiText-2\n84\t\n85\t  - id: plan_007\n86\t    claim: [1, 2, 3]\n87\t    description: >\n88\t      Evaluate on C4 perplexity (in addition to WikiText-2) for Qwen2.5-7B.\n89\t      Cross-dataset evaluation to show results are not WikiText-2 specific.\n90\t    priority: P0\n91\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n92\t    deps: []\n93\t    registry_id: null\n94\t    model: Qwen2.5-7B\n95\t    eval: C4\n96\t\n97\t  # === P1: Important, do if time allows ===\n98\t\n99\t  - id: plan_008\n100\t    claim: [2]\n101\t    description: >\n102\t      RateQuant comparison: implement RateQuant's greedy algorithm (Algorithm 1)\n103\t      on our discrete action set {2,4,8,16}-bit. RateQuant's Prop. 6 optimality\n104\t      relies on consecutive-integer polymatroid structure which breaks on non-consecutive\n105\t      sets. Show greedy produces suboptimal allocation vs constrained MCKP.\n106\t      Critical for differentiation claim — must have experimental evidence.\n107\t    priority: P0\n108\t    gpu_budget_hours: 4\n109\t    deps: []\n110\t    registry_id: null\n111\t    model: Qwen2.5-7B\n112\t    eval: WikiText-2\n113\t\n114\t  - id: plan_009\n115\t    claim: [2]\n116\t    description: >\n117\t      Oracle comparison: brute-force optimal allocation on a subset\n118\t      (3-4 layer groups) of Qwen2.5-7B. Quantify MCKP gap to oracle.\n119\t    priority: P1\n120\t    gpu_budget_hours: 6\n121\t    deps: [plan_006]\n122\t    registry_id: null\n123\t    model: Qwen2.5-7B\n124\t\n125\t  - id: plan_010\n126\t    claim: [2]\n127\t    description: >\n128\t      Cross-domain calibration robustness: calibrate on C4,\n129\t      evaluate on WikiText-2 (and vice versa). Report per-head\n130\t      allocation agreement rate across calibration sources.\n131\t    priority: P1\n132\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n133\t    deps: [plan_007]\n134\t    registry_id: null\n135\t    model: Qwen2.5-7B\n136\t\n137\t  - id: plan_011\n138\t    claim: [1]\n139\t    description: >\n140\t      Head sensitivity visualization: generate paper-quality figures\n141\t      showing per-head profiling delta heatmap across layers,\n142\t      compounding effect curve, and budget allocation comparison chart.\n143\t    priority: P1\n144\t    gpu_budget_hours: 1\n145\t    deps: [plan_004, plan_006]\n146\t    registry_id: null\n147\t\n148\t  - id: plan_014\n149\t    claim: [2]\n150\t    description: >\n151\t      K/V separation: treat K and V heads as independent MCKP items with\n152\t      separate budget allocation. Compare joint K+V optimization vs current\n153\t      uniform K=V approach. RateQuant supports asymmetric K/V (e.g. K=2.85,\n154\t      V=2.15 avg bits) — we should show MCKP naturally handles this.\n155\t    priority: P1\n156\t    gpu_budget_hours: 3\n157\t    deps: []\n158\t    registry_id: null\n159\t    model: Qwen2.5-7B\n160\t    eval: WikiText-2\n161\t\n162\t  # === P2: Nice-to-have ===\n163\t\n164\t  - id: plan_012\n165\t    claim: [1, 2]\n166\t    description: >\n167\t      Downstream task evaluation: ARC-C / HellaSwag / PIQA / WinoGrande\n168\t      on Qwen2.5-7B at 4× compression. Must match RateQuant's eval suite\n169\t      for direct comparison. Tests whether PPL improvements translate\n170\t      to downstream performance.\n171\t    priority: P1\n172\t    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n173\t    deps: [plan_005]\n174\t    registry_id: null\n175\t    model: Qwen2.5-7B\n176\t\n177\t  - id: plan_013\n178\t    claim: [1]\n179\t    description: >\n180\t      70B profiling-only: run distortion profiling on Qwen2.5-72B\n181\t      (no full eval). Analyze whether sensitivity patterns\n182\t      (Layer 0 dominance, compounding threshold) scale with model size.\n183\t    priority: P2\n184\t    gpu_budget_hours: 4\n185\t    deps: []\n186\t    registry_id: null\n187\t    model: Qwen2.5-72B\n188\t\n189\t# MVP experiments (already completed)\n190\tcompleted_mvp:\n191\t  - registry_id: exp_c_constrained_mckp\n192\t    claim: [1, 2, 3]\n193\t    result: \"PASS — PPL 11.23 vs uniform 15.45 (27%)\"\n194\t  - registry_id: p0_2_cliff_7B\n195\t    claim: [1]\n196\t    result: \"SUCCESS — Layer 0 cliff confirmed on 7B\"\n197\t  - registry_id: p0_2_cliff_1.5B\n198\t    claim: [1]\n199\t    result: \"SUCCESS — Layer 0 cliff discovered on 1.5B\"\n200\t\n201\t# Resource summary\n202\tresource_summary:\n203\t  total_p0_gpu_hours: 24\n204\t  total_p1_gpu_hours: 22\n205\t  total_p2_gpu_hours: 8\n206\t  available_gpus: \"2× RTX PRO 6000 96GB (westd-37397)\"\n207\t  estimated_p0_wall_time: \"2-3 days (parallel on 2 GPUs)\"\n208\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cxbwokq1XMvJjn87kQykrf","session_id":"6cf1809e-9145-4d61-9695-42edadd6799b","uuid":"74928cf8-7360-4f1d-99ce-1d9cc5d37e0e","timestamp":"2026-05-14T00:56:40.236Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HRvokjypkKjFjGPkNebn6Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013D33Axyduu7ohp21JKv3UC","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2) for a top ML venue peer review. Your focus is **Novelty and Related Work**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\"Discrete Mixed-Precision KV Cache Quantization via Constrained Multiple-Choice Knapsack\" proposes per-head KV cache bit-width allocation formulated as a constrained Multiple-Choice Knapsack Problem (MCKP) over discrete bit-widths {2, 4, 8, 16}. Key elements:\n- Distortion profiling: δ_h(b) = PPL(model; h→b) − PPL(model; FP16), measuring per-head quantization sensitivity\n- MCKP formulation: minimize total distortion s.t. one bit-width per head, global bit budget, cardinality constraint ≤k heads at 2-bit\n- The cardinality constraint is the key novelty: it regularizes the compounding effect (non-additive degradation when many heads simultaneously at extreme quantization)\n- Solver runs in polynomial time via DP, <2 minutes for H≤1000 heads\n\n## Claims\n1. Per-head sensitivity heterogeneity: L0 heads exhibit 42-100× higher profiling delta across Qwen/Llama/Mistral\n2. Constrained MCKP outperforms uniform: 12-27% PPL improvement at 4× compression\n3. Cardinality constraint as effective heuristic (not principled regularization): broad sweet spot k∈[8,24]\n\n## Related Work as Written\n- KV cache compression: KVQuant (per-channel), KIVI (asymmetric K/V), RateQuant (continuous waterfilling, per-head), H₂O/ScissorHands/SnapKV (eviction-based), ARKV (per-layer quant + eviction)\n- Mixed-precision quantization: GPTQ, AWQ for weights. Notes KV cache mixed-precision is less explored due to inference-time dynamic nature.\n- Knapsack in ML: NAS, filter pruning. Claims first application to per-head KV cache bit-width with cardinality constraints.\n\n## Key Results\n- Qwen2.5-7B: MCKP PPL 11.23 vs uniform 15.45 (27% improvement) at 4×\n- Llama-3.1-8B: 15% improvement, Mistral-7B: 12.1%\n- Waterfilling comparison: MCKP 11.52 vs discretized waterfilling 14.23 (19.1% advantage)\n- MCKP within 2% of brute-force oracle at 173× less compute\n- Downstream: 62% MMLU recovery, 58% LongBench recovery\n- At 2× compression, MCKP advantage is only 4.3%, paper acknowledges waterfilling may be competitive there\n\n## Your Review Task\nEvaluate **novelty** and **related work** critically. Address:\n\n1. **Novelty assessment**:\n   - Is the MCKP formulation genuinely novel? MCKP is a well-known optimization problem. The application to KV cache bit-width allocation is the novelty claim.\n   - How incremental is this over RateQuant? RateQuant already does per-head allocation via rate-distortion; this paper changes the solver (continuous→discrete) and adds a constraint.\n   - The cardinality constraint is acknowledged as an empirical heuristic, not principled. Does this weaken the contribution?\n   - Is the \"compounding effect\" observation itself novel or previously known?\n\n2. **Related work completeness**:\n   - Are important baselines missing? (e.g., SqueezeLLM, QuIP, AQLM for weight quantization; any recent KV cache mixed-precision work)\n   - Is the comparison with RateQuant fair? (using their distortion model projected to discrete, not their actual implementation)\n   - ARKV comparison: paper mentions it but doesn't compare experimentally\n   - Any concurrent/recent work on per-head KV cache quantization missing?\n\n3. **Positioning**:\n   - Does the paper clearly differentiate from RateQuant?\n   - Is the contribution positioned correctly (system contribution vs theoretical contribution)?\n\n4. **Significance**:\n   - Would this change how practitioners do KV cache quantization?\n   - Is the practical impact sufficient for a top venue?\n\nWrite a structured review with:\n- Summary (2-3 sentences)\n- Strengths (bulleted)\n- Weaknesses (bulleted, with severity: major/minor)\n- Questions for authors\n- Score (1-6 scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept)\n- Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous. Top ML venue acceptance rate is ~25%."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29761,"cache_read_input_tokens":22907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29761},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6cf1809e-9145-4d61-9695-42edadd6799b","uuid":"99d19a70-d1e1-46b9-ab60-338e241a263e"}
